# QA After Gameplay Changes (ABSOLUTE — ALWAYS ON)

**Mandatory.** The owner must not have to ask "did you run QA?" after combat, planning, sim, or ability work.

If this turn **changed gameplay systems** (see scope below), the agent **must run the matching automated QA suite(s)** and **report PASS or FAIL** in the turn **Changelog** before ending the turn. **Do not claim a fix is done without QA output.**

## What counts as a gameplay-system change

Any edit under these paths (or equivalent behavior owners):

| Domain | Typical paths / owners |
|--------|-------------------------|
| Simulation | `core/simulation/`, `Simulator`, `ResolutionPipeline`, `BoardState` / `UnitState` resolution |
| Combat systems | `core/systems/` (`AbilitySystem`, `MovementSystem`, `CombatSystem`, …) |
| Planning / commit | `presentation/combat_planning_input.gd`, `combat_director.gd`, commit slots, preview, drag/drop, undo |
| Abilities / data | `data/definitions/`, ability `.tres`, factories that affect combat legality or resolution |
| Presentation tied to sim | `tactical_unit_layer.gd`, `tactical_planning_overlay.gd`, planning cursor/icons when commit/preview semantics change |
| Tests that **fix** gameplay | Changing production code **and** tests together still requires running the suite |

**Not in scope (QA not required):** pure docs, `.cursor/rules`, menu/UI theming with no combat behavior, living-map/VFX-only slices (use phase visual gates from `roadmap.mdc` instead).

## Which suite to run

| Change touches | Run (headless) |
|----------------|----------------|
| Planning, preview, commit, drag, undo, cursor, overlay paths, `CombatDirector` refresh | **Planning QA gate (headless)** — `.\scripts\run_planning_qa_gate.ps1` **once** (default; **no** `-LiveTier3`). Runs SSOT + AOE + full headless fixtures (`PlanningQaGate.tscn`) + T3 bible mirror. **Do not** run `run_planning_scene_acceptance.ps1` unless the owner explicitly asks for live Tier 3. |
| Core sim / bridge / broad combat regression | **Full regression** — `.\scripts\run_regression_tests.ps1 -GodotPath "<godot.exe>"` |
| Both planning and core sim | **Planning QA gate** + **full regression** (two commands, one run each) |

### Class factory / skills / passives (`.cursor/rules/class-qa-standards.mdc`)

**Mandatory when touching** `core/factory/classes/`, class scenario registries, `docs/<CLASS>_QA_GATE.md`, `live_<class>_class_test.gd`, or claiming a class complete.

| Action | Run |
|--------|-----|
| Any class factory or per-class scenario change | `.\scripts\run_<class>_qa_gate.ps1` **and** `.\scripts\run_<class>_live_qa.ps1` |
| Changelog | Suite **PASS** / **FAIL** for the class you touched. Do not recite owner sign-off or LOCK. |

**Headless harness green alone is not class QA PASS.** Planning QA does not substitute for class gates.

### Focused swap iteration (mandatory while fixing swap)

When the turn is **only** fixing swap / walk-then-swap / swap commit presentation / swap preview parity:

| Do | Don't |
|----|-------|
| Run **`.\scripts\run_swap_planning_acceptance.ps1`** each fix attempt | Run `run_planning_qa_gate.ps1` or the full bible session until swap PASS |
| Report swap script **PASS** or **FAIL** with `[FAIL]` lines | Dismiss swap failures as "pre-existing" or unrelated |
| After swap PASS, run **`.\scripts\run_planning_qa_gate.ps1`** once before claiming the turn done | Stop at swap PASS if other planning files changed outside swap scope without re-gating |

Swap-only runner: GdUnit `test_live_swap_session` in `tests/live_planning_scene_test.gd` (ignores `test_live_planning_bible_multi_knight_session`).

When unsure, run **Planning QA gate** at minimum for anything in `presentation/combat_*` or planning input. Run **full regression** when `core/simulation/` or `ResolutionPipeline` changes.

**Run QA once per turn.** Re-run only if the suite **FAIL**s and you are fixing toward a new pass.

Authoritative checklist mapping: `docs/qa/planning/PLANNING_QA_GATE.md`.

## Agent workflow (every gameplay edit turn)

1. Implement the change.
2. **Run** the required suite(s) — agent executes the command; do not only tell the owner to run it.
3. **Changelog (mandatory):** under `### QA`, record:
   - Suite name(s) run
   - **Result:** `PASS` or `FAIL`
   - On FAIL: paste or summarize `[FAIL]` lines; **fix or stop** — do not hand-wave "should work"
4. **Commit** per `auto-commit-absolute.mdc` only after QA **PASS**, or after documenting FAIL with owner-approved deferral.

## Fail policy

- **FAIL → do not mark task complete.** Fix and re-run QA, or stop and report blockers.
- **QA-fix discipline (ABSOLUTE):** `.cursor/rules/global-systems-first.mdc` § QA Fix Discipline — fix the **canonical owner** (settle/slots/sim/director), never heuristic overlay fallbacks or per-test branches to chase green. Invalid plan → do not implement.
- **Never ignore Tier 3 `[FAIL]` lines** — every failure is in scope until fixed or owner explicitly defers.
- **Swap-only work:** iterate with `run_swap_planning_acceptance.ps1` until PASS; full gate only after swap is green.
- **Skipped QA → rule violation** (same severity as skipping auto-commit).
- **Manual Layer B** (F5 pixels, walk anim feel, FPS) remains the owner's job; headless PASS does not replace visual checks for animation/perf claims.

## Relationship to other rules

- **Parent:** `global-systems-first.mdc` — preview/commit parity tests live in planning QA.
- **Class work:** `class-qa-standards.mdc` — Knight-depth automated tests when you touch a class; planning QA is not a substitute. Kits are drafts.
- **Complements:** `roadmap.mdc` (phase gates), `move-preview-intent-truth.mdc` (drag E2E catches release path).
- **Wins over:** convenience, "small fix", ending the turn without running tests.
